<$fill $name="body">

!! Config

|!Tiddler |!Default |!Meaning |
|`$:/config/rimir/ports/enable` |`yes` |`no` removes handles, flyout and dock |
|`$:/config/rimir/ports/options/hide-archived` |shipped |Option source with filter `[!status[archived]]` for all ports |
|`$:/plugins/rimir/ports/default-option-filter` |`[!is[blank]]` |Filter used when no option source applies |

!! Option source tiddlers

Tagged `$:/tags/rimir/ports/option-source`.

|!Field |!Required |!Meaning |
|`filter` |yes |Runs on the port's candidates (`subfilter`), e.g. `[!status[archived]]` or `[tag[team]]` |
|`kind` |no |Only for ports of instances of this kind |
|`field` |no |Only for this field key |
|`ref-type` |no |Only for fields that accept this kind |
|`caption` |no |Shown in the dock footer and the settings |

The most specific matching source wins (score: `kind` 4, `field` 2, `ref-type` 1). One source per drag.

!! Drop target specs

Tagged `$:/tags/rimir/ports/target`. Shipped: `$:/plugins/rimir/ports/targets/dock-tile`, `$:/plugins/rimir/ports/targets/story-tiddler`.

|!Field |!Meaning |
|`selector` |CSS selector of elements that stand for a tiddler, e.g. `.tc-tiddler-frame[data-tiddler-title]` |
|`title-attribute` |Attribute of that element holding the tiddler title |

The innermost matching element under the pointer is the target. Classes set on targets: `ports-valid` (fits the dragged port), `ports-hover` (under the pointer), `ports-peek` (target of the hovered port), `ports-picked` (picked with Shift), `ports-picked-member` (a member a picked group adds). Every visible element of a title gets the class (a story tiddler and its dock tile). While Shift is held during a drag, `body` has `ports-collecting`.

!! Picking several targets

Only on multi-value fields; on single-value fields Shift does nothing.

|!Gesture (while dragging) |!Effect |
|Shift tap over a target |Picks it; over a picked target unpicks it |
|Shift held, moving |Picks the target under the pointer when Shift went down and every valid target the pointer moves onto (adds only, never unpicks) |
|Shift + letter |Types the capital into the search; the picks of that Shift hold are undone |
|Shift tap over nothing |No effect |
|Release over a target |Links all picks plus that target |
|Release over empty space |Links all picks; without picks the drag is cancelled, as before |
|Esc |Cancels the drag and all picks |

The drop is one write to the source tiddler. A picked group adds its members not yet linked, never itself; a title reached twice (picked on its own and via a team) is added once. One notification names what was linked and how many were already there.

!! Handle template variables

For bridges that put handles elsewhere (`$:/plugins/rimir/ports/handle`):

|!Variable |!Meaning |
|`ports-tid` |The instance |
|`ports-exclude` |Title list of ref fields to leave out |
|`ports-variant` |Adds class `ports-handle--<variant>`; `tiddler` is used in the story |

!! State

|!Tiddler |!Fields |
|`$:/temp/rimir/ports/flyout` |`src`, `exclude`, `expanded` (fields listing their targets), `show-empty` |
|`$:/temp/rimir/ports/drag` |`src`, `field`, `search`; with Shift picks also `picked` (title list), `picked-links` (titles the picks add), `picked-skipped` (already linked) |
|`$:/temp/rimir/ports/dock-search` |Search text when the dock is open by hand |
|`$:/state/rimir/ports/dock` |`open` while opened by hand |
|`$:/state/rimir/ports/recent/<field>` |`list` of the last 5 targets |

!! Engine functions

|!Function |!Returns |
|`ports.fields(type-tid, exclude)` |Ref field keys of the kind, in schema order |
|`ports.filled(type-tid, tid, exclude)` / `ports.empty(…)` |Ports with / without a value |
|`ports.values(type-tid, tid, field-key)` |Linked titles of one port |
|`ports.count(type-tid, tid, exclude)` |Number of links |
|`ports.option-source(type-tid, field-key, src-kind)` |Title of the option source that applies |
|`ports.candidates(type-tid, field-key, src, opt, q)` |Dock candidates: kind's ref candidates plus the groups whose members fit (`kind.ref-group-candidates`), minus the source, narrowed by the option filter and the search, sorted by caption (title when blank) |

!! Restart

`ports-layer.js` is a widget module: reload the browser page after changing it. Everything else refreshes live.

